Cloud Economics

Free Tier:- Certain services are always free, and some are free for 12 months after new account creation.
	    EC2 750 hr,  S3 5gb, RDS 750hr  all are for 12 months in free account.
	    DynamoDB 25gb, Lambda 1 millian, all for Always free
	    SageMaker 2 months.
	    
On Demand:- On-demand is full pricing and pay-as-you-go, but no contact and very flexible.
	    money = Size
	    Pay As you go.

Reservations:- Reservations are contracts that you enter with Amazon for 1-3 years.
	       It is the commitment to amazon to use it for the particular time like 1 -3 years.
	       You will have to pay if you use it or not.
	       Amazon give you the discount for using this type.

Volume Discount:- pay less per unit as you use more.
		  So As your wtorage goes up Amazon gives you discount as you consume more.
		  S3 1 cent for 1gb 
		  The more you use the lower it costs per unit.

Price Drop:-  Price drops are random price cuts that aws does every few years on its ervices.
	      Amazon drop the price of new services. 
	      since 2006 to 2013 aws drop prices of 129 times on varity of services.
	      Price drop suspecially the new version of servies comes up they drop price of per unit.
	      

